    "text": "Sume menn nyton gewiss, for heora nytennysse, hwi godspell is gecweden, o\u00fe\u00fee hw\u00e6t godspell\nGodspell is witodlice Godes sylfes lar, and \u00f0a word \u00fee he spr\u00e6c on \u00feissere worulde, mancynne to lare\nNu sceole we gehyran \u00fe\u00e6t halige godspell mid onbryrdnysse, us to beterunge, and eac we sceolon witan\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re Frigenihte \u00fee \u00e6tforan Eastron bi\u00f0 h\u00e6fde ure H\u00e6lend, \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee he \u00ferowode, swi\u00f0e langsume\nNe b\u00e6de ge nan \u00feing git on minum naman; bidda\u00fe and ge underfo\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t eower bliss beo full.\nIc spr\u00e6c to eow on bigspellum, ac nu bi\u00f0 se tima \u00fe\u00e6t ic on bigspellum eow to ne sprece, ac ic cy\u00f0e eow\nOn \u00feam d\u00e6ge ge bidda\u00f0 on minum naman geornlice, and ic ne s\u00e6de eow git \u00fe\u00e6t ic sylf wylle biddan\nSe sylfa F\u00e6der lufa\u00f0 eow, for \u00f0an \u00fee ge lufedon me, and ge gelyfdon \u00fe\u00e6t ic fram Gode ferde.\nIc ferde fram \u00feam F\u00e6der and com to middanearde; ic forl\u00e6te eft middaneard and ic fare to \u00feam F\u00e6der.\n\u00dea s\u00e6don his folgeras mid swi\u00f0licre blisse, Efne \u00feu sprecst nu swutellice, leof, and \u00feu nateshwon ne\nNu we witon so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu wast ealle \u00feing, and \u00fee nis nan neod \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee hwa ahsige; on \u00f0am we\nWe habba\u00f0 nu ges\u00e6d sceortlice on Englisc \u00feis halige godspell, swa swa ge gehyrdon nu, \u00fea nacedan\nSo\u00f0, so\u00f0 ic eow secge, gif ge sylfe hw\u00e6s bidda\u00fe \u00e6t minum halgan F\u00e6der eow on minum naman, he hit\nSe H\u00e6lend w\u00e6s gehaten fram his cildhade Iesus, fram \u00feam halgan engle, \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee he acenned wurde,\nBide \u00fee nu h\u00e6lu on \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes naman, modes and lichaman, o\u00fe\u00fee for leofne freond, and se F\u00e6der\nGif \u00f0u \u00feonne yfel bist, \u00feu most yfeles geswican, and to \u00feam